    {
      "id": "lTS4dnTJPyAjzNlBVYsGr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3559.973616182153,
      "y": 12343.557650888946,
      "width": 693.1995239257812,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCh",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1475646531,
      "version": 962,
      "versionNonce": 1285938947,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773661973607,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. ALL AGREED\nID Tables (TableID) are synced to databricks after its parent stream\ncompletes execution so that no new ID is generated in\ndatabricks (in ideal scenario where logic matches 1:1) \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. ALL AGREED\nID Tables (TableID) are synced to databricks after its parent stream\ncompletes execution so that no new ID is generated in\ndatabricks (in ideal scenario where logic matches 1:1) \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "M4TVPFVMC0JfmIz6RKzwE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3404.1778832201894,
      "y": 12809.125524856983,
      "width": 921.3795776367188,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCi",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 305561709,
      "version": 1739,
      "versionNonce": 1924304535,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1774953815197,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "7. finalized\nFor Hybrid Tables, for simple scenarios, where there are no parallel writes, \nthe hybrid target table (Table 12) is synced daily just before the current \nTD stream(TD Stream 1) run in TD, so that DBX stream has the latest copy of the \"target\"\ntable. Reconcilation is performed against copy of Table 12 in DBX against \ntarget copy of TD stream 1 of TD.\nFor streams using this as a source, we will need to sync this tables daily until\nall of its producers are migrated.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "7. finalized\nFor Hybrid Tables, for simple scenarios, where there are no parallel writes, \nthe hybrid target table (Table 12) is synced daily just before the current \nTD stream(TD Stream 1) run in TD, so that DBX stream has the latest copy of the \"target\"\ntable. Reconcilation is performed against copy of Table 12 in DBX against \ntarget copy of TD stream 1 of TD.\nFor streams using this as a source, we will need to sync this tables daily until\nall of its producers are migrated.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
